# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in one key. `.env` is gitignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Every model in Stantal is optional. With no key at all it still runs and still
# reports — Layer 1 findings that depend on meaning are marked `unconfirmed`
# instead of confirmed, and Layer 2 does not run. A key upgrades the answer; it
# is never required to get one.

# Pick ONE of these. The first key present wins unless STANTAL_JUDGE or
# STANTAL_CALLER says otherwise. Both layers read the same three.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Layer 1: the judge ------------------------------------------------------
#
# Answers one closed yes/no/unclear question per finding, and must quote the
# text it relied on. The quote is checked against the source, so a fabricated
# justification is discarded rather than reported.

# Force a provider, or turn the judge off entirely: anthropic | openai | gemini | none
# STANTAL_JUDGE=anthropic

# Override the model. Worth setting for a backfill: walking a whole release
# history on the priciest model is waste.
#   anthropic default: claude-opus-5
#   openai    default: gpt-5.4-mini
#   gemini    default: gemini-3.6-flash   <-- pinned, see below
# STANTAL_JUDGE_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5

# How the request is sent: auto | http | sdk
# `auto` uses the vendor SDK when one is installed and plain HTTP otherwise.
# Both send the same prompt and are checked the same way, so this only changes
# retries and error typing — never what counts as a finding.
# STANTAL_JUDGE_TRANSPORT=auto

# Point at a proxy or a compatible endpoint.
# STANTAL_JUDGE_BASE_URL=

# --- Layer 2: the behavioural caller -----------------------------------------
#
# Shows a model each version's contract and records the tool call it makes.
# Nothing is executed: no credentials, no side effects. Off unless asked for —
# it costs k calls per intent per side, so an available key is deliberately not
# enough to start spending.

# Force a provider, or turn Layer 2 off: anthropic | openai | gemini | none
# STANTAL_CALLER=openai

# Override the model.
#   anthropic default: claude-sonnet-5
#   openai    default: gpt-5.4
#   gemini    default: gemini-3.6-flash
#
# The caller and the judge default to different OpenAI models on purpose. The
# judge answers a closed question whose quote is verified mechanically, so a
# mini model is safe there. The caller has to stand in for whatever a real host
# runs, and a mini model would make the findings unrepresentative.
# STANTAL_CALLER_MODEL=gpt-5.4

# STANTAL_CALLER_BASE_URL=

# OpenAI only: request cheaper, slower processing. Opt-in and UNVERIFIED —
# nobody has confirmed against the live API that it changes anything, which is
# exactly why it is not a default.
# STANTAL_SERVICE_TIER=flex

# --- Gemini through Vertex AI ------------------------------------------------
#
# AI Studio (the GEMINI_API_KEY above) and Vertex serve the same models and are
# billed separately. Only Vertex draws on Google Cloud credits. Set a project
# and both the judge and the caller route there instead.
#
# This is a TRANSPORT, not a provider: the id stays `gemini:<model>`, so every
# cassette recorded through AI Studio still answers a question asked through
# Vertex. Same model, same body, same reply — only the address and the way the
# request is signed differ. Verified against the live API 2026-08-26.
#
# STANTAL_VERTEX_PROJECT=my-gcp-project
#
# Location defaults to `global`, and should usually stay there: measured,
# us-central1 returns 404 for the current flash models.
# STANTAL_VERTEX_LOCATION=global
#
# Auth is an OAuth token, not an API key. Left unset, the gcloud CLI is asked
# for one (`gcloud auth login` first). Tokens last about an hour, so supply one
# directly for CI or for a long backfill:
# GOOGLE_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# --- The caches --------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Every reply is written to disk and keyed on the TEXT of the question or
# request, so the same one is never paid for twice. Measured on a 46-release
# walk: 66 questions, 2 HTTP requests cold, 0 warm.
#
#   record  (default) serve from disk, call for anything new, save the reply
#   replay            serve from disk only — cannot call out, so it cannot spend
#   off               no cache
#
# `replay` is what CI and the test suite should use. It makes spending a token
# by accident impossible rather than merely unlikely.
# STANTAL_JUDGE_CACHE=record
# STANTAL_BEHAVIOUR_CACHE=record

# Where cassettes live. Both default under .stantal/ (gitignored).
# STANTAL_JUDGE_CACHE_DIR=.stantal/judge
# STANTAL_BEHAVIOUR_CACHE_DIR=.stantal/behaviour

# --- Why gemini is pinned ----------------------------------------------------
#
# A cache key includes the model id. Every judge cassette on disk was recorded
# against `gemini:gemini-3.6-flash`, and this project's reported findings replay
# from those recordings with no key and no network call at all. A newer
# gemini-3.7-flash exists and works — moving the pin would strand every
# recording and force the whole judged history to be answered again, so it has
# not moved. OpenAI's default moved because gpt-4o was two generations stale.
#
# The same rule applies to every default here: changing one abandons whatever
# was recorded under the old id. That is silent by design — a miss just calls
# out again — so check before you bump.
